satisfied|content|ADJECTIVE|pleased with a result|Feeling that something meets your needs or expectations well enough.|hài lòng|The customers were satisfied with the repair and collected their bicycles.|Khách hàng hài lòng với việc sửa chữa và đến nhận xe đạp.|Satisfied with names what meets expectations; does not necessarily mean delighted or perfect.|0
wish|want-unreal|VERB|want a different situation|To want a situation to be different, especially when changing it is difficult or impossible.|ước; mong|I wish the bus came more often on Sundays.|Tôi ước xe buýt chạy thường xuyên hơn vào Chủ nhật.|Wish plus a past form can describe an unreal present situation; the past form need not indicate past time.|0
wish|desire|NOUN|something wanted|A desire for something to happen or be true.|mong ước; điều ước|Her wish was to see the sea with her grandparents.|Mong ước của cô ấy là được ngắm biển cùng ông bà.|Countable; a wish to do something names a desired action, while a wish for names the desired thing.|1
wish|goodwill-message|NOUN|expression of hope for someone|An expression of hope that someone will have happiness or success.|lời chúc|They sent their best wishes to the couple before the wedding.|Họ gửi những lời chúc tốt đẹp nhất đến cặp đôi trước lễ cưới.|Often plural in best wishes or good wishes; distinct from a private desire.|2
choir|singing-group|NOUN|group singing together|An organized group of people who sing together.|dàn hợp xướng|The choir practised quietly in the hall before the concert.|Dàn hợp xướng tập hát khẽ trong hội trường trước buổi hòa nhạc.|Countable; choir names the group, while chorister names a member.|0
hail|praise|VERB|publicly praise as important|To publicly welcome or praise someone or something as important or successful.|ca ngợi; hoan nghênh|The reviewers hailed the exhibition as a fresh approach to local history.|Các nhà phê bình ca ngợi triển lãm là một cách tiếp cận mới đối với lịch sử địa phương.|Transitive hail something as something; this sense involves public evaluation, not frozen rain.|0
hail|weather|VERB|fall as balls of ice|For small balls of ice to fall from the sky.|mưa đá|It began to hail just as we reached the bus shelter.|Trời bắt đầu mưa đá đúng lúc chúng tôi tới nhà chờ xe buýt.|Intransitive weather verb, normally with it as the grammatical subject.|1
hail|call-vehicle|VERB|signal for a vehicle to stop|To call or signal to a vehicle so that it stops for you.|vẫy gọi xe|He hailed a taxi outside the station.|Anh ấy vẫy gọi một chiếc taxi bên ngoài nhà ga.|Transitive in hail a taxi; the object is the vehicle being called.|2
index|measure|NOUN|number indicating change or level|A number used to show the level of something or how it changes.|chỉ số|The index rose after the new figures were published.|Chỉ số tăng sau khi các số liệu mới được công bố.|Countable; an index of a measured quality names what is represented, not a list of book entries.|0
index|book-list|NOUN|list for finding information|An ordered list of subjects or names with references showing where to find them.|bảng tra cứu; mục lục tra cứu|Use the index to find the pages about water storage.|Dùng bảng tra cứu để tìm các trang nói về việc trữ nước.|Countable; usually at the back of a book, unlike a contents list of chapters.|1
